{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"61537f4a19bb237010665c585cdea4cf72c74f851dee08bed66f6ac18aa23c59","slug":"ch01.intro","location":"/ch01/intro.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"第一章 原子的核式结构","content_includes_title":false,"authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Jin Lei","given":"Jin","family":"Lei"},"name":"Jin Lei","url":"https://jinlei.fewbody.com","id":"contributors-myst-generated-uid-0"}],"github":"https://github.com/jinleiphys/atomic","numbering":{"title":{"offset":1}},"source_url":"https://github.com/jinleiphys/atomic/blob/main/book/ch01/intro.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/jinleiphys/atomic/edit/main/book/ch01/intro.md","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"intro.md","url":"/atomic/build/intro-eb2079b893f54b4840ad17970deacdfb.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"物质可以无限分割吗？","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"xt2lHmPZ6q"}],"identifier":"id","label":"物质可以无限分割吗？","html_id":"id","implicit":true,"key":"BbSh86rMgN"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"拿起一块石头，把它掰成两半。再把其中一半掰成两半。继续下去，一直掰，一直分——这个过程能永远进行下去吗？你最终会得到什么？","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"c0KeiqRqQi"}],"key":"JktWoGbmma"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"这个看似天真的问题，困扰了人类最优秀的头脑两千五百年。公元前五世纪，古希腊哲学家德谟克利特给出了一个斩钉截铁的回答：不能。他认为，分割到某个尺度之后，你会得到一种不可再分的最小微粒，他把它叫做 atomos，希腊语中\"不可切割\"的意思。在德谟克利特看来，整个宇宙不过是这些不可分割的微粒在虚空中运动、碰撞、组合的结果。一切宏观现象——水的流动、火的燃烧、生命的诞生与消亡——归根结底都是原子排列方式的变化。","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"poEy8LrHXQ"}],"key":"ebdiI5OwPf"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"但同时代的另一位巨人亚里士多德完全不同意。他认为物质是连续的，可以无限分割下去，永远不会到达某个\"最小单元\"。空间是满的，不存在虚空。在亚里士多德看来，德谟克利特的原子论在逻辑上就有问题：如果原子是有大小的实体，那它就有左半边和右半边，就应该可以继续分割；如果原子没有大小，那无穷多个没有大小的东西怎么能组成有大小的物体？","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"YP8MNtjfPa"}],"key":"XztdjbwaqI"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"这场争论的本质是一个深刻的哲学问题：","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"zg72Pj8Oy0"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"自然界的基本构成是离散的还是连续的？","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"CYuFhUt1fT"}],"key":"UYw7IPlVoP"},{"type":"text","value":" 用现代的数学语言说，物质的结构更像整数还是更像实数？整数是一颗一颗分开的，之间有间隙；实数是连绵不断的，任意两个数之间还有无穷多个数。如果物质是\"整数型\"的，那就存在最小单元；如果物质是\"实数型\"的，那分割可以永远进行下去。","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"PWPqkFDVT1"}],"key":"AfB3G0DM1F"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"有趣的是，这个问题在纯粹的哲学框架内是无法回答的。你无法通过逻辑推演来判断物质到底是离散的还是连续的——两种可能性在逻辑上都是自洽的。亚里士多德的论证和德谟克利特的论证一样精妙，双方打了个平手。这场僵局持续了两千多年，直到人类发明了一种新的判定方式：实验。","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"key":"HYCgxhbsjS"}],"key":"xlpUl3wMIV"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"硅基视角：计算机中的数可以无限小吗？","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"key":"Ogv85t5znZ"}],"identifier":"id","label":"硅基视角：计算机中的数可以无限小吗？","html_id":"id-1","implicit":true,"key":"hZxJN350XJ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"\"离散还是连续\"这个古老的哲学之争，在计算机的世界里有一个出人意料的现代翻版。","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"Her6sXSmLG"}],"key":"myZC2Ry1X9"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"在数学中，实数是连续的。在 0 和 1 之间有无穷多个数，在 0.1 和 0.2 之间也有无穷多个数，无论你把区间缩得多小，其中永远包含无穷多个实数。然而，当我们试图用计算机来表示实数时，立刻就撞上了一堵墙：计算机的底层是晶体管，晶体管只有两种状态——开和关，0 和 1。用有限个比特去表示无穷多个实数，注定是一场不可能完成的任务。","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"Oqs047QW6k"}],"key":"HMHycWuIqF"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"计算机的解决方案是浮点数。IEEE 754 标准定义了两种最常用的格式：单精度(float32)用 32 个比特存储一个数，双精度(float64)用 64 个比特。以单精度为例，32 个比特被分成三个部分：1 位符号位决定正负，8 位指数位决定数量级，23 位尾数位决定精度。这意味着单精度浮点数在整条数轴上总共只能表示大约 ","position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"key":"pyCFvSRhxY"},{"type":"inlineMath","value":"2^{32} \\approx 4.3 \\times 10^9","position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"html":"<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>32</mn></msup><mo>≈</mo><mn>4.3</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>0</mn><mn>9</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2^{32} \\approx 4.3 \\times 10^9</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">32</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">4.3</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">9</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>","key":"IrEGeRIB59"},{"type":"text","value":" 个不同的数。听起来很多，但和实数的无穷相比，这不过是沧海一粟。","position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"key":"VB9HyHv3rq"}],"key":"n7I1sPDA1E"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"这带来一个直接的后果：浮点数之间存在间隙。两个相邻的浮点数之间，有无穷多个实数是无法被精确表示的。这种间隙的大小用机器精度(machine epsilon) ","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"key":"ecbvZOKRQH"},{"type":"inlineMath","value":"\\varepsilon","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"html":"<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ε</span></span></span></span>","key":"UsYC87EPYt"},{"ty